        "main_text_has_explicit_synthesis": true,
        "si_used": false,
        "procedure": "All syntheses were performed under aerobic conditions. Gd(NO3)3·6H2O (113 mg, 0.25 mmol), H2L (122 mg, 0.5 mmol), PhCOOH (61 mg, 0.5 mmol), and NEt3 (1.5 mmol) were added to MeCN (20 mL); NiCl2·6H2O is the nickel source used in the 1:1:2:2 Ni:Gd:H2L:benzoic acid reaction. The green solution was stirred for 60 min, filtered, and left to evaporate undisturbed at room temperature. Yellow-green single crystals of 1·13.6MeCN·H2O formed after 2 days (~40% yield), were collected by filtration, and dried in air. Elemental analysis was reported for the desolvated composition 1·4MeCN.",
