      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility (300–2 K, 0.1 T) shows ferromagnetic intramolecular coupling. Room-temperature χmT is 46.13 cm3 mol−1 K (Curie expectation 44.21 cm3 mol−1 K for 4 NiII + 5 GdIII with gNi=2.2, gGd=2.0). χmT is nearly constant to ~50 K then rises to 109.43 cm3 mol−1 K; magnetization saturates at 43.0 μB. Heat-capacity and magnetization data give a magnetocaloric effect: for ΔB=7 T, −ΔSm reaches 10.7 R (19.2 J kg−1 K−1) at 3.3 K and ΔTad reaches 7.3 K at 2.3 K, so adiabatic demagnetization from 9.6 K and 7 T to 0 T cools the sample to 2.3 K.",
