      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "magnetic",
        "summary": "Dc susceptibility (300–2 K, 0.1 T) indicates dominant ferromagnetic Ni–Ni exchange. Room-temperature χmT is 4.82 cm3 mol−1 K (Curie 4.84 cm3 mol−1 K for 4 NiII, diamagnetic Y). χmT is nearly constant to ~50 K, rises to 9.41 cm3 mol−1 K, then drops near 5 K to 8.93 cm3 mol−1 K at 2 K. Magnetization saturates at 8.4 μB. Simultaneous PHI fit of χmT and M vs B: J1 = +5.26(9) cm−1, J2 = +2.26(1) cm−1, D1 = −10.86(10) cm−1, D2 = 3.90(3) cm−1, g = 2.21, zJ′ = 0.",
